From: Jannis Leidel <jannis@leidel.info>
Subject: [PATCH] Normalize macOS wheel tags

Normalize the macOS deployment target used for the wheel platform tag.

Starting with macOS 11, wheel platform tags only carry the major version
(e.g. macosx_11_0_arm64, macosx_12_0_arm64). A deployment target such as
"11.3" or "12.1", coming from MACOSX_DEPLOYMENT_TARGET or from sysconfig,
would otherwise produce a tag like "macosx-11.3-arm64" via
_PYTHON_HOST_PLATFORM, which does not match what pip and packaging expect
and can yield a wheel that is not installable on the intended systems.

Clamp the minor version to ".0" for deployment targets >= 11, and leave
10.x targets (where the minor version is significant) untouched.

diff --git a/api/python/backend/setup.py b/api/python/backend/setup.py
--- a/api/python/backend/setup.py
+++ b/api/python/backend/setup.py
@@ -74,6 +74,9 @@
         deployment_target = os.getenv(
             "MACOSX_DEPLOYMENT_TARGET", None
         ) or sysconfig.get_config_var("MACOSX_DEPLOYMENT_TARGET")
+        # Wheel tags use only the major macOS version from macOS 11 onward.
+        if deployment_target and int(deployment_target.split(".")[0]) >= 11:
+            deployment_target = f"{deployment_target.split('.')[0]}.0"
         os.environ["_PYTHON_HOST_PLATFORM"] = (
             f"macosx-{deployment_target}-{config.osx_arch}"
         )
